## Fragmentation Considerations

- **Internal fragmentation**: Inherent in fixed-size bucketing; acceptable given latency requirements
- **External fragmentation**: Mitigated by pre-allocated slabs and lazy reclamation (freed objects held until next allocation)
- **Cross-node fragmentation**: Remote frees accumulate in target node queues; monitored via periodic compaction

## TLB/Cache Effects

- Slab allocation ensures objects within a slab share TLB entries
- Cache-line-aligned objects prevent false sharing in multiprocess workloads
- Large pages (2MB/1GB) recommended for bulk allocations to reduce TLB pressure
- NUMA interleaving disabled for hot paths; manual placement preferred

